I continue to find people's obsessive delineation of Tale vs. SCP to be absurd.
附加记录：    

The 'hook' of this site is that the format of most of our fiction is that of a scientific document. Wanting the scientific documents to remain looking like scientific documents because traditional prose has a place in tales is not absurd.

It's because an SCP article is something that exists in-universe in a specific format, not as a traditional narrative. These half-tale-with-no-reason-for-the-format-screw articles do not make sense in-universe and OOU they're taking up SCP slots with blatant tale format.

I don't want it to sound like I don't think things like this have a place on the site (the votes prove I'm in the minority on seeing it as that big of an issue) but our site is growing extremely quickly and format screw SCPs that have no logical, in-universe reason to be a format screw are not helping the numbers, IMO.




Seconding MacWarren on overall article opinion.





