Oh boy. I'm not quite sure what to say. It's rough around the edges, in ways that I can't quite elaborate upon without rereading this behemoth. There's also waxing and waning in my interest from section to section. Learning what a few farmhands have to say about a glue factory just isn't as interesting as getting a look at Clef's head. But overall you've got this well-written, well not quite epic, per se. It needs a bit more closure than what here's right now. But you got me invested and you got me intrigued and I really did want to read more and more. The novelty of redefining the lore is handily backed up by a tight central narrative, and I hope that the next part of series doesn't take too long to come out! I do hope that it's a bit tighter and bit less dithering next time, though.








